Here's a simple C++ function that uses the `pugixml` library to parse markdown text and convert it to HTML. This function assumes that you have the `pugixml` library installed and linked to your project.

```cpp
#include <pugixml.hpp>
#include <string>

std::string markdown_to_html(const std::string& markdown_text) {
    pugi::xml_document doc;
    pugi::xml_parse_result result = doc.load_string(markdown_text.c_str());

    if (!result) {
        // Handle parsing error
        return "";
    }

    pugi::xml_node root = doc.document_element();
    std::string html_text;
    pugi::xml_print_settings settings;
    settings.m_indent = 0;
    pugi::xml_writer_settings writer_settings;
    writer_settings.m_indent = 0;
    pugi::xml_writer writer(&html_text, writer_settings);
    root.print(writer, settings);

    return html_text;
}
```

You can use this function like this:

```cpp
int main() {
    std::string markdown_text = "# Hello World!";
    std::string html_text = markdown_to_html(markdown_text);
    std::cout << html_text << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This will output: `<h1>Hello World!</h1>`

Note: You need to install the `pugixml` library and link it to your project.

